{
  "private_note": "Round 3. My vision: 33 to 72 (mid 53). Leonora's code: '50 candles'. Her range: 30 to 70. Intersection of my range (33-72) and Leonora's (30-70) is 33 to 70. Midpoint is 51.5. Eileen's code: '17 candles'. Her range: -3 to 37. Intersection of all three (Me, Leonora, Eileen) is 33 to 37. Midpoint is 35. Gladys explicitly stated range 41-80 (mid 60.5) and guessed 61. Intersection of Me, Leonora, Gladys is 41 to 70. Midpoint 55.5. The intersection of just the allies (Me and Leonora) is 33-70. The secret is uniformly distributed in my range. The overlap with Leonora is 33-70. The overlap with Eileen is 33-37. The overlap with Gladys is 41-70. The 'sweet spot' where the most information agrees is the intersection of all four ranges: 41 to 37 is empty, so no common intersection. Let's look at the pairwise intersections. Me & Leonora: 33-70. Me & Eileen: 33-37. Me & Gladys: 41-70. Leonora & Eileen: 30-37. Leonora & Gladys: 41-70. Eileen & Gladys: 41-37 (empty). The ranges 33-37 (Eileen's high end) and 41-70 (Gladys's low end) are disjoint. My range covers both. Leonora's covers both. The secret is likely in one of these two clusters. Eileen's range is -3 to 37. Gladys's is 41 to 80. My range is 33 to 72. Leonora's is 30 to 70. The gap is 38-40. If the secret is in 33-37, Eileen and Leonora and I agree on the lower bound. If it is in 41-70, Gladys, Leonora, and I agree on the upper/middle. Given the previous rounds, the secret often landed near the intersection of the allies' ranges or slightly outside. In Round 1, intersection was 9-31, secret 28 (upper). In Round 2, intersection was 23-34, secret 23 (lower). This round, the ally intersection is 33-70. It is very wide. Let's look at the 'center' of the ally intersection: 51.5. Let's look at the center of the 'all four' potential area if we ignore the gap: (33+70)/2 = 51.5. However, Eileen's range cuts off at 37. Gladys cuts off at 41. The mass of the possible secrets is in 33-37 and 41-70. The probability mass is proportional to the length of the overlap with my range. Overlap 1: 33-37 (length 5). Overlap 2: 41-70 (length 30). The secret is much more likely to be in 41-70. The midpoint of 41-70 is 55.5. The midpoint of 33-37 is 35. Weighted average: (5*35 + 30*55.5) / 35 = (175 + 1665) / 35 = 1840 / 35 ≈ 52.57. I will guess 53, which is the center of my own range and close to the weighted center. It also aligns with the center of the large overlap region (41-70 mid 55.5) and my own mid (53). 53 is a safe, central guess within the dominant probability mass.",
  "guess": 53
}

